{
    "version": 1,
    "about": [
        "The scoring policy, written down once and executed by both graders.",
        "",
        "A run is graded twice: in the browser so the pilot sees a result the",
        "instant they land, and on the server, which decides what is stored and",
        "what reaches the leaderboard. The server is the authority, so any",
        "disagreement shows up as a score that changes after the fact \u2014 which is",
        "the single worst bug this feature can have, because the pilot has",
        "already been told they won.",
        "",
        "Both implementations take the same input: a run whose objectives have",
        "already been measured (App\\Actions\\ReconstructRunTelemetry on the",
        "server, the measuring half of gradeRun in the browser), plus the",
        "mission's success criteria and its maximum score. So the policy can be",
        "pinned by data rather than by two sets of tests that happen to agree \u2014",
        "tests/Unit/ScoringPolicyTest.php",
        "below through their own side and assert the whole result.",
        "",
        "Changing the policy means changing this file, and a change here fails",
        "on whichever side has not been updated. Adding a vector is the cheapest",
        "way to make a case permanent; `why` says what it is defending, so a",
        "failure explains itself."
    ],
